# Project Map: Durable CEO Directive Intake

Status: active
Type: project-map
Updated: 2026-09-12
Next Action: materialize PRM-0052 and execute M1-DURABLE-CEO-INTAKE
Source Idea: IDEA-0032
Source Directive: Make CEO directives support durable batch intake and non-preemptive interleaving through existing planning order and subordinate cycles

## Purpose

Let the CEO issue several durable directives before choosing one for implementation, and let new
directives arrive while implementation is underway without displacing the working subordinate
cycle. Reuse the canonical Idea planning order and outcome lineage instead of introducing a second
queue or a second source of scheduling authority.

## Settled Direction

- A previously unseen `ts: 100k add` or `ts: directive` command performs intake only: preserve the
  exact directive as an executive Idea, open its outcome, append it to existing planning order, and
  stop after a durable checkpoint.
- Reissuing the exact command for an active stored directive is the explicit delegation/resume
  action and continues through the existing Plan Cycle, PRM, campaign, evidence, and outcome chain.
- If another subordinate campaign is working, intake and resume requests do not preempt it. The
  requested directive remains queued in planning order unless the CEO explicitly changes order.
- The CEO projection is active-first in planning order, reports queue position and inventory
  truncation explicitly, and retains recent completed directives only after active directives.
- The bounded hosted payload remains advisory and read-only; local Tool Shed state stays canonical.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Route semantics | Separate durable intake from exact-match delegation/resume | existing directive route |
| Planning semantics | Preserve append order and the one-working-campaign invariant | canonical planning order |
| CEO projection | Active-first bounded inventory with position and explicit truncation | project projection |
| Hosted contract | Backward-compatible schema update for the richer directive inventory | CEO projection |
| Proof | Route, ordering, projection, contract, dashboard, and repository validation | prior workstreams |

## Completion Boundary

Complete at Work1 when local source, contracts, documentation, tests, generated views, and Hybrid
checkpoint prove durable multi-directive intake, exact-match delegation, non-preemptive
interleaving, and bounded active-directive visibility. Do not deploy, push, release, report the
candidate externally, or synchronize installed clients.
